checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-05-r9-records.md:1:**Minor · residual, row 2, where-this-sits.** “The Associated Press's 68,000 a month is 2026 so far, and its 9,700 is 2025.” The pinned [PAYEMS series](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/PAYEMS-2026-10-03.csv:1033) contains “2024-12-01,158316”, “2025-12-01,158432”, and “2026-09-01,159044”. Those levels yield about 9,700 jobs a month in 2025 and 68,000 in January through September 2026. The sentence credits AP for averages already available from the pinned payroll data. [AP reports the same figures](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/coverage/ap-september-jobs.txt:28); it is not a second payroll count. This source-authority finding first appeared in the [r1 red-team report](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-03-r1-redteam.md:3). The [ledger records the later pace-sentence patch](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/working-notes/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.md:760), but the attribution remains.
