The 13 blocks have two **Minor source-authority findings**. I found no Critical or Major defect. The later [BLS employment archive](https://www.bls.gov/bls/news-release/empsit.htm), [JOLTS archive](https://www.bls.gov/bls/news-release/jolts.htm), and [FOMC release list](https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/2026-press-fomc.htm) show no subsequent release or decision that makes a scoped sentence false.

1. **Minor, residual | Row 11, where-this-sits.** “The Associated Press said average job growth was an average 68,000 jobs a month so far this year, against its 9,700 average new jobs created every month in 2025.” The pinned [PAYEMS series](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/PAYEMS-2026-10-03.csv:1033) gives “2024-12-01,158316”, “2025-12-01,158432”, and “2026-09-01,159044”. Those levels yield both averages. The sentence adds no unsupported number, but credits AP for figures available from the pinned primary payroll series. [AP’s pin](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/coverage/ap-september-jobs.txt:28) reports the same figures; it is not a second payroll count. This issue first appeared in the [r1 red-team report](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-03-r1-redteam.md:3). The [ledger’s later pace patch](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/working-notes/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.md:773) leaves the attribution in this block.

2. **Minor, new | Row 1, what-happened.** “Reuters wrote that government payrolls contracted 17,000, mostly in local government, excluding education.” The pinned [BLS release](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:1722) gives “| Government | 23,568 | 22,138 | 22,499 | 23,355 | 23,543 | 23,300 | 23,344 | 23,327 | -17 |” and [its local-government row](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:1731) ends “| -10.6 |” for local government excluding education. The sentence adds no unsupported amount, but credits Reuters for a breakdown carried by the pinned primary. The correct account is a 17,000 government payroll decline, of which 10,600 was in local government excluding education.

Blocks checked: 13; findings: Critical 0, Major 0, Minor 2.
